  "recommendation": "PROCEED",
  "verdict_line": "The BILL LBO delivers a 3.7x MOIC and 30% IRR anchored by a defensible 10.0x entry multiple, a proven 15% EBITDA growth trajectory, and only modest exit multiple expansion required to achieve target returns. Despite the flagged uncertainty on the exit multiple, the organic growth and cash generation profile provide sufficient downside cushion to support a proceed decision.",
  "thesis_sections": [
    {
      "title": "Summary",
      "paragraphs": [
        "We are acquiring BILL at a $2.5B enterprise value, representing a 10.0x entry EBITDA multiple \u2014 a defensible valuation for a scaled SMB payments and financial operations platform. With $1.625B of sponsor equity deployed and a 3.5x debt/EBITDA capital structure, the base case projects a 3.7x MOIC and 30% IRR at exit, driven by organic EBITDA growth and modest multiple expansion."
      ],
      "cited_claims": [
        {
          "assumption_id": "entry_ev",
          "value": "2.5e+09",
          "phrase": "$2.5B enterprise value"
        },
        {
