          "phrase": "3.7x MOIC"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "irr",
          "value": "0.3",
          "phrase": "30% IRR"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Value creation",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Organic growth is the primary engine. BILL's embedded position in SMB accounts payable and receivable workflows, combined with its network effects across suppliers and accountants, supports a 15% annual EBITDA growth rate through volume expansion, cross-sell of spend management and payments products, and continued platform monetization. This trajectory is consistent with the company's established growth history in a structurally underpenetrated market.",
        "Margin expansion reinforces the growth story. BILL's SaaS-like revenue model and high incremental margins on transaction volumes allow operating leverage to materialize as the platform scales. A 65% free cash flow conversion rate reflects disciplined working capital management and limited capex intensity, enabling meaningful debt paydown over the hold period and compounding returns to equity.",
        "At exit, we underwrite a modest re-rating from 10.0x to 12.0x EV/EBITDA, consistent with peer comps for high-growth fintech platforms demonstrating durable unit economics. This multiple expansion, combined with EBITDA compounding, drives exit enterprise value to approximately $6.0B, delivering the targeted return profile."
      ],
      "cited_claims": [
        {
