    {
      "title": "Risk factors",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The most material risk is the exit EV/EBITDA assumption of 12.0x, flagged at 55% confidence given a thin peer sample for comparable fintech platforms. A compression to 10.0x at exit \u2014 no re-rating \u2014 would materially reduce equity proceeds and compress returns below target. Additionally, fintech sector risks include SMB credit cycle sensitivity reducing transaction volumes, competitive pressure from bank-embedded AP/AR solutions, and regulatory scrutiny on payments infrastructure that could increase compliance costs and compress FCF conversion from the assumed 65%."
      ],
